flowchart TD
    I[Researcher intent] --> C[Markdown research contract]
    C --> R[YAML experiment recipe]
    R --> S[Session state + profile snapshot]

    subgraph DECL[Declarative / Control Plane]
      C
      R
      S
      PC[policyctl boundary]
      AU[Append-only audit]
      BB[Blackboard / durable case state]
    end

    S --> A[Primary agent adapter]
    A --> PC
    A --> ORCH[Primary-agent native orchestration]

    subgraph AGENT[Multiagentic Operator Plane]
      ORCH --> ROLES[Specialist role recipes]
      ROLES --> PL[Planner]
      ROLES --> RE[Researcher]
      ROLES --> RA[Runtime analyst]
      ROLES --> FO[Forensics]
      ROLES --> DE[Detection]
      ROLES --> AN[Analysis]
      ROLES --> VE[Independent verifier]
      ROLES --> RG[Report generator]
      ORCH --> SK[Versioned skills]
      ORCH --> MCP[Scoped MCP tools]
    end

    subgraph GW[Model / Routing Plane]
      RT[Declared routing]
      LT[LiteLLM]
      OM[OmniRoute]
      RT --> LT
      RT --> OM
    end
    A --> RT
    ORCH --> RT

    PC --> AP[Approval gate]
    AP --> VM[Disposable Lima / QEMU VM]

    subgraph EXEC[Controlled Execution Plane]
      VM --> IN[Instrumentation]
      IN --> WK[Approved workload]
      WK --> EV[Telemetry + raw evidence]
    end

    EV --> BB
    BB --> AR[Evidence + hashes + provenance]
    BB --> AN
    AN --> VE
    VE --> RR[Research report]
    RG --> RR

    subgraph LEARN[Optional Learning Plane]
      RR --> LI[Identify reusable improvement]
      LI --> TF[Optional Taskflow]
      TF --> REF[Evaluate / refine candidate]
      REF --> LG[Optional LangGraph]
      LG --> RP[Replay]
      RP --> VE
      VE --> HA[Human approval]
      HA --> PR[Promote validated skill / recipe improvement]
    end

    RR --> PRES[Preserve evidence]
    PRES --> TD[Finalize token/session dashboard]
    TD --> DEST[Destroy disposable VM]
    DEST --> DONE[Complete session]

    S --> AU
    PC --> AU
    EV --> AU

    SEC[VM / OS controls] -. enforce isolation .-> VM
    OBS[Agent observability: Numbat + Phoenix/OTel + Aegis] -. observe .-> A
    OBS -. observe .-> EV

    classDef declarative fill:#eef6ff,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
    classDef agent fill:#fff7ed,stroke:#ea580c,stroke-width:2px
    classDef gateway fill:#f0fdf4,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef evidence fill:#f5f3ff,stroke:#7c3aed,stroke-width:2px
    classDef security fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#15803d,stroke-width:2px
    class C,R,S,PC,AU,BB declarative
    class A,ORCH,ROLES,PL,RE,RA,FO,DE,AN,VE,RG,SK,MCP agent
    class RT,LT,OM gateway
    class AR,RR,LI,TF,REF,LG,RP,HA,PR evidence
    class VM,SEC security

    %% Invariants: recipes are authoritative; role recipes remain semantic specialist definitions; primary agent owns orchestration; policyctl is outside the agent control plane; gateways/agents/skills/MCP/observability are not security boundaries; Lima/QEMU + VM/OS enforce workload isolation.
